1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:02,201
You asked for Rogers City, Michigan.

2
00:00:02,431 --> 00:00:04,483
In one night, 33 men were lost.

3
00:00:04,713 --> 00:00:06,969
23 of them were from this small town.

4
00:00:07,619 --> 00:00:09,224
November 1958.

5
00:00:09,454 --> 00:00:11,565
The Bradley, a limestone freighter more

6
00:00:11,575 --> 00:00:14,624
than 600 feet long, left Gary, Indiana,

7
00:00:14,634 --> 00:00:17,580
empty, bound for Calcite, at Rogers City.

8
00:00:17,980 --> 00:00:19,802
On Lake Michigan the next day, winds

9
00:00:19,812 --> 00:00:21,468
topped 60 miles an hour.

10
00:00:21,698 --> 00:00:23,750
Waves were about 25 feet high.

11
00:00:24,200 --> 00:00:26,697
Around 5:30 that evening, the Bradley

12
00:00:26,707 --> 00:00:27,388
broke in two.

13
00:00:28,188 --> 00:00:30,347
A Mayday went out, just as the power

14
00:00:30,357 --> 00:00:30,770
failed.

15
00:00:31,000 --> 00:00:33,985
Of 35 men aboard, 2 survived, on a raft,

16
00:00:33,995 --> 00:00:34,709
through the night.

17
00:00:35,259 --> 00:00:37,963
In Rogers City, more than 50 children lost

18
00:00:37,973 --> 00:00:38,642
their fathers.

19
00:00:39,392 --> 00:00:42,110
Today, a sailors' memorial by the lake in

20
00:00:42,120 --> 00:00:44,049
Rogers City lists the crew's names.

